    "result_text": "The full test suite consists of the single `AcceptanceTest` (the other files are the base class and an audit-log helper, not test classes). The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the tenure requirement for membership level 4 in `OwnerMapper.membershipLevel`:\n\n- The pre-tenure factors (base 1, +1 for email, +1 for `namesakeCount == 0`) are still capped at **3**.\n- Level **4** is now granted only when the owner's tenure \u2014 the days from `registrationDate` to the current date \u2014 **exceeds 365 days**, then capped at 4.\n\nSince a newly created owner's `registrationDate` is set to the current business day (zero tenure), a new owner never satisfies the `> 365` condition and therefore never exceeds level 3 \u2014 matching the acceptance test `coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3`, which expects a new owner with an email and no namesakes to be level 3.\n\n`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
